<title>UK: British brewers lobby European parliament.</title>
<headline>British brewers lobby European parliament.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Robert Neame, chairman of Britain's oldest brewer Shepherd Neame, delivered a petition to the Europeean parliament in Brussels on Thursday on behalf of independent brewers angered by the different levels of beer duty across Europe.</p>
<p>Neame arrived outside parliament's main entrance on a horse-drawn dray, the traditional way of delivering beer to British pubs.</p>
<p>The 38 independent family brewers across Britain are concerned that the high taxes on beer will lead to significant job losses in vulnerable regions.</p>
<p>The petition says that the wide discrepancies in excise duty between EU member states on alcholic drinks, and beer in particular, also distorts competition, encourages fraud and leads to a loss of revenue to governments.</p>
</text>
